**`GroupDIT`** — `src/test/java/com/intermarche/fidelity/e2e/GroupDIT.java`, report at `reports/e2e-D.md`.

Result (`mvn -q verify -DskipUTs=true -Dit.test=GroupDIT -DskipITs=false`): **10 run, 0 failures, 0 errors, 1 skipped**.

All ten D scenarios are implemented at the RestAssured/`@QuarkusTest` tier (none is `[W]` or `[P]`):
- **D1** nominal 201 + `expiresAt` = now+900s TTL; **D2** renewal 200 (pushed, amount modifiable, re-checked vs balance); **D3** 409 empty body; **D4** 404 empty body; **D5** the three 422s (`INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE`/`DAILY_RULE`/`ACCOUNT_STATUS`); **D7** confirm→dated negative BURN, idempotent, 404, 410; **D8** the 410 catch-up via `ticket-closed` + `EXPIRED_LEASE_CONFIRMED` trace warning; **D9** DELETE always 204 + balance freed + no daily-rule consumption; **D10** natural expiry frees the card.

**Blocker (one line):** D6 is `@Disabled` — `ReservationService.reserve()` checks the one-card conflict guard before the available-balance guard and renews against `balance` not available, so `25 € → INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE` on `…088` is structurally unreachable without a `src/main` change (out of scope); documented as justified residue.

Isolation is maintained throughout: the seeded `…088` lease is restored after D2, scratch-card reservations/movements are cleaned per test with balance recompute, every `ticketRef` is nanotime-suffixed, and all temporal behaviour is driven by aging `expiresAt` rows / `DateTimeProvider`, never the run clock. Only the generated test class and the report were touched; `src/main` was not modified.
