## Summary

I wrote `src/test/java/com/intermarche/fidelity/e2e/GroupIIT.java` covering all 6 group-I scenarios (UI Règles) and drove it to **6/6 green**:

- **I1** (RestAssured) — four state badges, clickable codes, `Éditer` only on UPCOMING, no `Fermer` button.
- **I2 [W]** (Playwright) — read-only sheet frozen (backbone + schema fields disabled), live Form/JSON toggle, "facteur cent" (rate shows **5** / JSON stores **0.05**), lock re-applied after the JSON→Form re-render.
- **I3 [W]** (Playwright) — schema-driven form regenerated per type, invalid-spec notice, same-code window-overlap notice.
- **I4** (RestAssured) — edit refused on an in-force rule (303 + literal), UPCOMING form live with frozen code, past-start refused.
- **I5** (RestAssured) — end-of-application block absent/present, set / clear / past-date / ended-frozen notices.
- **I6** (RestAssured) — duplication prefill (`_V2`, type, spec) and taken-code guard, type+spec copy verified in DB.

**Contract facts honoured:** seeded rules only read (isolated `ZZZ_*` test rules minted/purged for the UPCOMING/INACTIVE states the seed lacks); clock frozen via `DateTimeProvider` so windows are literal and never calendar-flaky; English literal notices asserted verbatim; DB reads via Panache under `QuarkusTransaction`, never by absolute id.

**One iteration** to green: Playwright `innerText()` returns CSS-transformed text (`.schema-scope-title` is `uppercase`), so I switched the `#schema-fields` content checks to `textContent()`.

**Justified residue** (documented in `reports/e2e-I.md`): I5's *sixth* sub-assertion — the `updateEndDate` "overlap another instance of code" notice — is genuinely **unreachable**: `FidelityRule.code` is `unique=true`, so no two same-code rows can coexist and the guard's overlap loop can never find a sibling. I reported it rather than fake it or touch `src/main`. The reachable variant of that literal (create-time overlap) **is** asserted in I3.

Report written to `reports/e2e-I.md`.
