## Summary

I wrote `src/test/java/com/intermarche/fidelity/e2e/GroupQIT.java` covering group Q — the "relevé PAR LE CODE" inventory of contractual literals and surfaces — and looped it to green:

```
mvn -q verify -DskipUTs=true -Dit.test=GroupQIT -DskipITs=false
→ Tests run: 9, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0
```

**9 `@Test`s, each carrying its Q-x id in name + Javadoc**, driving every literal end-to-end at the right tier:
- **Q-A** — 11 POS-API status/body couples (`/earn`, burn reservations, ingestion, accounts, batches) over Basic `pos`/`admin`.
- **Q-B** — the five-code closed warning nomenclature and its `CODE` vs `CODE:<ean>` trace formats (`UNKNOWN_EAN` on projection + trace, the four ingestion-only codes on their traces).
- **Q-C** (3 tests: rules/cards/communities) — every `AdminException` literal on a channel that reaches it, with `Unknown rule type …` and `Unknown card …` proven on **both** GraphQL and UI.
- **Q-D0** — per-resource CSV import row errors + the mechanic report proven valid JSON.
- **Q-D** — the ~19 English UI notices read off the un-followed 303 `Location`.
- **Q-E** — the French login/reset/confirm/simulator texts + drag-drop hint.
- **Q-F** — the boot lines (via `BootLogCapture`) and the per-request log lines.

All mutations target isolated `ZZZ_Q_*`/minted cards purged in `finally`; the seeded world is untouched; time is frozen at 2026-08-22.

**Two justified residues** (documented in-code and in the report, no `src/main` touched):
- `The new window would overlap another instance of code '<c>'` is structurally unreachable — `FidelityRule.code` is `@Column(unique=true)`, so a code never has a second instance for the overlap loop to find.
- `Empty database detected — loading the 2026 program seed` is the prod `SeedLoader` path and never fires under the dev/test DataInitializer boot; Q-F asserts its **absence** instead of flakily awaiting it.

Report written to `reports/e2e-Q.md`. There were no `[P]` scenarios in group Q, so nothing is `@Disabled`. Only the generated test class and the report were added.

One out-of-scope observation (reported, not acted on): GraphQL `setActivation` resolves as an undefined Mutation field even though `FidelityGraphQLApi` declares it — I routed that guard through the equivalent UI card-activation channel; it may be worth a look separately.
Done. `GroupQIT` is written and the campaign is green.

